  the plume measures wind speed to sigma = 0.095 %
  matching that from a fuel map alone would require the fuel spread rate
  known to 0.084 % -- about 417x better than an operational fuel model (~35 %).

  at a realistic 35 % fuel prior the arrival-time forecast spans 8 minutes;
  the plume collapses that to under a minute.

